{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1225073-pact-with-rabszolga-very-rough-sorcerous-initiation-outline","id":1225073,"title":"Pact With Rabszolga (Very rough Sorcerous Initiation outline)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-05T13:51:18-07:00","id":1225073,"title":"Pact With Rabszolga (Very rough Sorcerous Initiation outline)","content":"My Eclipse caste player has been trying to find a patron for sorcery, and based on where his character is heading, how he's been playing, etc none of the as written initiations seemed fitting, so I set out to cobble together a new one with Rabszolga the god of slaves as the source. I'm awful with mechanics, so its mostly a reworked Bargain With Mara, but I'd appreciate some more mechanically sound insight. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Whenever the Sorcerer takes a shape sorcery action while within medium range of a character with a Tie of subservience (or a similar emotion) towards her, she may reap additional sorcerous motes equal to that Intimacy\u2019s value (for example, four motes from a Defining Tie). Intimacies can only be tapped for motes in this fashion once per day. Normally she may only drain one Intimacy to fuel the casting of a spell, but she may draw power from any available Intimacies when casting her control spell. She cannot draw more than ten sorcerous motes per scene with this ritual. Rabszolga draws upon the power of those enslaved, however, and that exchange is not mutual. A Sorcerer cannot draw upon this wellspring of power while they are themselves bound in any way.<br /> <br /> A slave\u2019s life is worth only the value its master can draw from their investment, and is often easier to replace the slave than any goods they tend to. The Sorcerer can harvest power from those in their possession, drawing out their spark of life and creativity to power their workings, but at the cost of leaving their subject an empty, compliant husk not unlike the dream-eaten victims of the Raksha. The Sorcerer marks their subject as their property, with a brand, tattoo, or other permanent marking, on their Manipura chakra. Once completed, as the Sorcerer withdraws their hand they pull their subject's essence out with it. The The soul shard manifests as wrought iron key that glows faintly in the presence of the sorcerer. The victim must already be property of the Sorcerer before the process begins, as well as have a Major or Defining Intimacy of subservience their master. As a miscellaneous action, the sorcerer may offer up one of her bound souls to Rabszolga in exchange for power once per scene, rolling (Essence + Willpower) and gaining that many sorcerous motes. She retains these motes until the end of the scene, and may spend them towards any spells she casts. Additionally, a bound soul may be reflexively expended in place of a point of Willpower when paying the cost of the sorcerer\u2019s control spell. She cannot have more than (Essence + Occult) souls bound to her at one time. The subjects of this power become, for all intents and purposes, one of the dream-eaten. While still alive, they are only useful for the simplest and most repetitive, or dangerous, of tasks. Even a broken slave can have value to their master, to the right buyer.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer is made stronger the more individuals they claim. Once per scene, when another character forms or strengthens a Tie of subservience (or similar emotion) to the Sorcerer, the Sorcerer may draw power from their bending to her will, gaining sorcerous motes equal to the new intensity of the Intimacy. Bending beings of power to the Sorcerer\u2019s will is a particularly intoxicating and potent act. An entity of Essence 2 or higher doubles the sorcerous motes provided if the Intimacy in question is increased to either a Major or Defining severity. This skill has its limits, however, and beings with an Essence of two or more above the Sorcerer\u2019s provide only the normal benefit to sorcerous motes.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":".  Minor mechanical/thematical revisions 06-06-2018, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3